  "notes": "Paper by N. Crescini (arXiv:2311.16364) presents a new measured exclusion limit on the axion-electron pseudoscalar coupling gp using a radiofrequency fermionic (spin) interferometer with NiZn ferrimagnetic arms (~5.5 MHz resonances). The exclusion plot (Fig. 5) spans roughly 1e-11 to 1e-8 eV in axion mass, but the only explicit numerical value in the text is the best limit |gp| = 1.2e-7 at m_a ~ 0.36 neV (3.6e-10 eV), which is the single data point emitted. Assumes local DM density 0.4 GeV/cm^3; limit quoted at 2-sigma (90% CL). Confidence limited because the full exclusion curve is only available graphically, not in a table. | vector-trace candidate: gp_exclusion_plot.pdf colour (0.0, 0.39, 0.0), 92 pts (selected among 2) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 92))",
